\pard\b\fs20 Relic Hunt\b0\par
\fs16\par
The din of battle - a pause - then the trumpets sound again for the next attack: that is how it has gone here for ages. The wars of faith between the rival orders keep getting worse, and yet so far neither side has managed to take and hold the enemy's castle. But now that will come to an end, for the researching mages have gained new knowledge: the power of the elements! In this hotly contested holy land there are still ancient mythical ruins of a long-forgotten culture. This ancient people was able to compress each of the 4 forces of nature into an object. United, these four elementals would have the power to force the enemy to retreat, to occupy the castle and to claim this special land as one's own!\par
A new, exciting fight for the elementals outside both castles can begin!\par
This team melee has room for up to 12 players. A team has won when all four elementals have been safely deposited in front of its own sanctuary. The most sensible approach would surely be for one player from each team to try to claim the relics in the middle before seeing to the elementals divided between the two teams.\par
To get all the relics, an attack on the enemy castle will also be necessary, and anything is possible there: a direct air attack by airship, trying to get to the sanctuary through the earth, or quite simply blowing up the towers.\par
Castle buildings cannot be rebuilt. Buildings cannot be saved from burning down with the Extinguish spell.\par
The flying barrel is protected from fire arrows, but it needs quite a lot of fuel.\par
